{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794655405,"nonce":"y0uvjuOLJ/tPWoXjQpVybjyQhzo=","message":"Progress, and what changed from the plan above.\n\nSteps 1-3 (table, kinds, API): merged in #76.\n- Kinds are a discriminated union in the API (shared/schemas.ts AnnotationContent): audio {url} and text {text} (1-2000 characters, any note or translation). A new kind is a variant there; no migration.\n- The database doesn't check kinds or their data (only that data is a JSON object): SQLite can't change a CHECK without rebuilding the table (closed 8f43c94; the rest of the CHECKs are 4fb7d7b).\n- GET takes ?from=\u0026to= (UTF-16 offsets) and returns the annotations overlapping [from, to), so the reader can ask for the part it shows. Stores take (filter, page).\n- The cap (MAX_ANNOTATIONS, 2000) is read from user_document.annotations_count, kept by triggers, in the insert itself. Duplicates are skipped with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING; the result type is AnnotateResult (added / exists / full).\n- Timestamps are addedAt / added_at (CLAUDE.md).\n- No lenient parse of unknown kinds yet: the reader (step 6) needs one, so an old reader skips a kind it doesn't know.\n- An annotation's author is left out or non-empty (#79).\n\nStep 4 (curated): #79, open. inline texts only, not wolnelektury. Spans are marked Pandoc's way in the text, [some words]{label}, and annotations: maps each label to one annotation or a list (AnnotationCredit + AnnotationContent), in block YAML. Paragraph numbers and start/end in the file were dropped for this. sync-curated adds and removes annotations by id; --check lists them.\n\nStep 5 (Storybooks narration): branch storybooks-narration, stacked on #79. 420 clips over the 40 stories, read from each story page: its clips (page n's clip is NN.mp3, 01 is the title), its 'Read by:' (Helena Gabriela on all 40) and its licence. Licence decided: each recording gets its story's licence, since the page's one CC notice covers 'this work' (the page, its text and its recordings) and matches the file's licence on all 40. Source: the story page. Every paragraph matched its page's text except Liczymy zwierzęta's typo fix (see 4eba0cc); all 420 URLs return 200; the 42 inline texts keep their document ids.\n\nStep 6 (reader): not started. Render arbitrary kinds, starting with audio and text.","files":null}]}